    {
      "title": "Initial Packets",
      "desc": "The Client Hello, straight away",
      "detail": "There is no separate TCP handshake: the very first packets carry the TLS Client Hello. With its post-quantum key share it is 1,880 bytes, too big for one packet, so it fills two Initial packets. Each datagram is padded to at least 1,200 bytes; a server may send back only three times what it has received, so a forged sender address can’t turn it into an amplifier.",
      "facts": [
        [
          "Datagrams",
          "2 × 1,250 bytes"
        ],
        [
          "Carries",
          "The TLS Client Hello"
        ],
        [
          "Readable?",
          "Yes (Initial keys are public)"
        ]
      ],
